  "answer_text": "Here's a roundup of the **best laptop deals online right now** across different categories and budgets:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\uded2 Where to Shop for Laptop Deals\n\nYou can find all kinds of deals across a wide range of online retailers such as **Newegg, Walmart, Best Buy, Amazon**, and so on. It's also worth checking out deals directly from laptop manufacturers like **Lenovo, HP, and Dell**.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udcbb Top Laptop Deals Right Now\n\n### 1. \ud83c\udfc6 Best Overall \u2013 Lenovo Yoga (2-in-1)\nThe Lenovo Yoga features a **14-inch 2880\u00d71800 OLED display** with HDR up to 120Hz, powered by an **Intel Core Ultra 7 258V CPU, 32GB of RAM, 1TB SSD**, and Intel Arc 140V graphics. It weighs under three pounds, offers up to **23 hours of battery life**, and flips all the way around so you can use it like a tablet or prop it up like a tent.\n\n---\n\n### 2. \ud83d\udcb0 Best Budget Pick \u2013 Dell 15 Laptop\nNeed an affordable laptop for the basic stuff? The **Dell 15 Laptop** is the one to spring for \u2014 its **AMD Ryzen 3 7320U** chip is well suited for daily tasks like browsing, streaming, and email.\n\n---\n\n### 3. \ud83c\udfae Best Gaming Deal \u2013 RTX 5060 Lenovo Gaming Laptop\nThis **RTX 5060 Lenovo gaming laptop** is one of the best deals of the week \u2014 featuring an **OLED display, Ultra 7 chipset, 32GB of RAM**, and **$400 off**.\n\n---\n\n### 4. \ud83c\udf4e Best MacBook Deal \u2013 Apple MacBook Air (M4/M5)\nSave up to **$300 on the Apple MacBook Air** \u2014 with two unmissable deals on the **M4 and M5** models currently available.\n\n---\n\n### 5. \ud83d\udda5\ufe0f Best High-Performance Picks on Best Buy\nBest Buy currently features hot options like the **ASUS ROG Zephyrus G16** (Intel Core Ultra 9 285H, RTX 5070, 16GB RAM), the **MSI Stealth A18 AI+** (RTX 5080, 32GB RAM), and the **HP OmniBook X Flip 2-in-1** (Intel Core Ultra 5, 16GB RAM, 512GB SSD).\n\n---\n\n### 6. \ud83d\udcb8 Best Extreme Savings\nOne standout deal is a **14-inch laptop with Core Ultra 7 255H and RTX 5060** priced at **$1,099** (down from $2,599) \u2014 a massive **$1,500 savings**. There's also a **Snapdragon X2 Plus** model for **$1,199** (was $1,899), saving you **$700**.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udca1 Tips Before You Buy\n\n- Aim for at least **8GB of RAM** (16GB is preferable, especially for gaming). Avoid laptops with under **4GB of RAM or 128GB of SSD storage**.\n- **Chromebooks** make great everyday machines for browsing and email \u2014 they use fewer resources and are generally more affordable than Windows laptops.\n- A **Windows laptop** is far more versatile and can be configured with a ton of RAM and storage for power users.\n\n---\n\nFor the latest and most up-to-date deals, visit:\n- \ud83d\udd17 [PCWorld Laptop Deals](https://www.pcworld.com/article/550968/best-laptop-deals-3.html)\n- \ud83d\udd17 [Best Buy Laptop Sales](https://www.bestbuy.com/site/all-computers-tablets-on-sale/laptops-on-sale/pcmcat1720704669400.c)\n- \ud83d\udd17 [TechRadar Best Laptop Deals](https://www.techradar.com/news/the-best-laptop-deals)\n- \ud83d\udd17 [HP Weekly Deals](https://www.hp.com/us-en/shop/slp/weekly-deals/laptops)\n- \ud83d\udd17 [BestLaptop.Deals](https://www.bestlaptop.deals/)",
